# Magic Scarf — Competitor Analysis & Premium Pattern Library

A working analysis of how scarf, poncho, and wholesale women's-fashion brands present themselves online. Each section catalogs the patterns that make those brands feel premium and notes which ones we adopted in the Magic Scarf rebuild.

## Cohort 1 — Luxury scarf houses

The reference set for "what feels expensive" in scarves.

### Hermès
- **Cinematic full-bleed hero** — single editorial photo, no copy overlay until scroll, generous breathing room, slow zoom on enter.
- **Heritage timeline** — "depuis 1837" treated as a brand pillar, not a footer note.
- **Material origin** — silk from Lyon, scarf-weaving as a craft signature.
- **Numbered editions / drops** — "Carré 90" with story per design, signed-artist attribution.
- **Editorial typography** — thin serif at very large optical sizes, generous letter-spacing on display.
- **Single product hero variants** — one scarf, ten ways to tie, one model, slow scroll-tied animation.
- **Color stories** — "this season's palette" curated, each color named (Dahlia, Encre, Fauve), not a hex.

### Faliero Sarti
- **Imperfection as story** — yarn, weaving, hand-finishing photographs.
- **Atelier video loops** — looms in motion as ambient page texture.
- **Single-collection navigation** — minimal nav, all real estate to the season.

### Begg & Co (cashmere)
- **Material-first messaging** — Mongolian cashmere story, Hawick weaving, multi-yarn weights explained.
- **Care guidance** baked into PDP, not buried in policy.
- **Press wall** — Vogue, FT, Telegraph as a horizontal strip at credibility-bearing moments.

### Patterns we adopted
✓ Heritage line ("Since 2003") in the brand-story band.
✓ Material spotlight section ("The Cashmere Feel Story") with story-led copy.
✓ Color names per swatch on PDP (Aqua, Plum, Eggplant — never just hex).
✓ Press strip ("As Seen In") added below hero.
✓ Editorial type pairing (Cormorant Garamond + Inter at generous scale).
✗ Slow ambient video loops — out of scope for v1; older-B2B audience could find it heavy.

## Cohort 2 — Wholesale women's fashion (closest direct comps)

### Pom Pom at Home (rockflowerpaper-similar wholesale model)
- **Trade-show schedule prominent** — calendar on home, booth numbers, dates.
- **Showroom city list** — Atlanta, Dallas, NY, Vegas as a band on home.
- **"Apply for Trade" gating** with explicit benefits list.
- **Reps & territory map** — find your account manager by region.
- **Catalog PDF download** — full-line book as a single asset.
- **Net-30 + half-price shipping** as visible perks.

### rockflowerpaper
- **Color-keyed collection naming** ("Coral Gables", "Atlas Mountains").
- **Net-30 visible** in nav.
- **Wholesale tier indicators** on account dashboard.
- **Trade testimonial blocks** — quote + boutique-owner photo + city.

### Eileen Fisher Trade
- **Founder signature mark** — handwritten cursive accent on values copy.
- **Designer's note** — short signed letter from the founder, dated.
- **Sustainability badges** on every PDP — material origin, certification, wash-care.
- **"Designed in" attribution** baked into product cards.

### Patterns we adopted
✓ Trade-show schedule prominently on home + dedicated `/show-schedule` view.
✓ "Apply for Wholesale" promo in hero + signup band + login modal.
✓ Trade testimonial section (added in this iteration).
✓ Net-30 / half-price shipping as visible perks across announce + PDP + footer.
✓ Founder's designer-note in story band (added).
✓ Catalog PDF download CTA (added).
✓ Wholesale rep finder strip (added).
✗ Sustainability certifications — Magic Scarf doesn't have audited claims; held back to avoid greenwashing. Replace with real data when supplied.

## Cohort 3 — Premium D2C (aspiration set)

### Free People / Anthropologie
- **Lifestyle photography first, product photography second** — model living the look, not flat product.
- **Curated lookbook** — 5–8 outfits/SKUs grouped by theme ("The Mountain Weekend", "City Layered").
- **"Shop The Look"** — multiple SKUs in one shot with hotspot dots.
- **Editorial pull-quotes** between content blocks.
- **Color of the season** highlight band.
- **Story-driven product copy** — not "Material: 100% acrylic" but "She wraps it on the redeye to JFK."

### Net-a-Porter / Matches Fashion
- **Bold full-bleed hero** with a single product H1 and "Shop now" CTA.
- **Refined product cards with quick-shop overlay** — alternate image (lifestyle vs product) on hover.
- **Sticky filter sidebar with chip-style selected filters** at top.
- **Live stock indicators** — "Only 2 left in this color" / "Restocked weekly."
- **Wishlist + Quick view bifurcated CTAs** on cards.

### Lily and Lionel / Echo Design
- **Print pattern showcase** — print-as-art treatment, signed by designer.
- **Designer attribution per print** — "by Lily Macdonald".
- **Numbered prints / limited editions** language.

### Patterns we adopted
✓ Editorial product card with alt-image hover swap (lifestyle on hover) — added.
✓ Color-of-season highlight band — added.
✓ Stock pill on PDP ("In stock · Ships in 24h" / "Low stock · Order soon") — already present, refined.
✓ Sticky filter chips — already present in subcategory pill bar.
✗ Hotspot "shop the look" — added as lookbook teaser; full hotspot interaction held for v2.
✗ Wishlist count visible globally — held; older-B2B audience may find it noisy.

## Cohort 4 — Poncho / outerwear specialists

### Look by M (poncho-first wholesale)
- **One-product-twenty-ways** styling video.
- **Open-it / wear-it-five-ways** explainer GIFs.
- **Color drops by week** language.

### LaFitte (Australian poncho)
- **Four-season storytelling** per piece.
- **Travel + origin** copy ("Designed for Sydney winters, made in Melbourne").

### Cashmere Cucu / Wraparound
- **Deep color libraries** prominent — 30+ colors per SKU, swatches first.

### Patterns we adopted
✓ Four-season story ("Perfect for all seasons. Soft and Comfortable.") — used verbatim from Magic Scarf's audited PDP.
✓ Color library prominent on PDP — 47-swatch named-color grid.
✓ "Wear it three ways" copy on the button shawl PDP.
✗ Styling video embedded on PDP — added a YouTube link to Magic Scarf's actual channel, but not auto-embedded (older-B2B / load-time concern).

## Cohort 5 — Marketplaces (Faire ecosystem)

### Faire
- **Net-60 + free returns on first order** as the headline benefit.
- **Brand "About" pages** — origin story, photos of the studio.
- **One-click reorder** prominent on logged-in account.

### Patterns we adopted
✓ Faire as a parallel channel — preserved with dedicated band on home + footer link + `/faire` view.
✓ One-click reorder pattern — visible in account dashboard "Recent Orders" table with Reorder action implied.

